# eFootball Champions League settings (Django version).
# Copy this file to ".env" (next to manage.py) for local use, and set the same names as
# environment variables on your host (Koyeb: Service → Settings → Environment variables).
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Never commit or share your real .env – it holds passwords.

# ---------- Must set in production ----------
# A long random secret for signing logins. Generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(50))"
# SECRET_KEY=
# Public address of the site (no trailing slash). Used for emailed links, allowed hosts and secure cookies.
# APP_URL=https://your-app.koyeb.app
# 1 when the site runs behind a host/proxy (Koyeb, Railway, Render, Fly, Caddy, Nginx).
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# ---------- Database ----------
# Where the league is stored. On hosts whose disk is wiped on restart (free Koyeb), use a Postgres
# database, e.g. a free one from neon.tech. Paste its connection string here:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxxx.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/league?sslmode=require
# Without DATABASE_URL a local SQLite file is used (default: data/league.sqlite3; change with DB_FILE).
# DB_FILE=/data/league.sqlite3

# ---------- First admin / password reset ----------
# On start the account is created, or its password reset, when ADMIN_PASSWORD is set (10+ characters).
# After you can log in, REMOVE ADMIN_PASSWORD and change the password in the Admins tab.
ADMIN_USER=boss
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose a long password
# ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com

# ---------- Email for invites and password resets ----------
# Recommended: Brevo (free, 300/day). It sends over HTTPS, so it works on hosts that block email ports.
# 1) Sign up at brevo.com  2) Senders → add and verify your email  3) SMTP & API → API keys → create one.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=brevo
# EMAIL_API_KEY=xkeysib-...
# EMAIL_FROM=eFootball League <you@gmail.com>
#
# Other choices: EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend (needs your own domain), smtp (below) or console (prints to the log).
# SMTP example for Gmail – needs an App Password; some hosts block these ports:
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASS=abcd efgh ijkl mnop

# ---------- Optional ----------
# Your time zone, used to group public results by day (visitors always see their own local times).
# TIME_ZONE=Africa/Accra
# PORT=3000
# Extra host names the site may be reached on (comma separated). APP_URL's host is added automatically.
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=league.example.com
# Starting league for a brand-new database (default: seed.json next to manage.py).
# SEED_FILE=/data/seed.json
# Folder for `python manage.py backup` (default: data/backups).
# BACKUP_DIR=/data/backups
# Force secure cookies (normally automatic when APP_URL starts with https).
# COOKIE_SECURE=1
